    "result_text": "That's a JaCoCo coverage exclude, not a test exclude. The full suite ran and passed.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented address normalization following the existing `TelephoneNormalizer` precedent, keeping structural impact minimal.\n\n**New file \u2014 `util/AddressNormalizer.java`:** a small, cohesive utility (`normalize` + private `expand`) that trims, collapses internal whitespace, upper-cases, and expands `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`. It's null-safe, returns `\"\"` for blank input, and is idempotent (so create and duplicate-detection share one canonical form).\n\n**Changed 3 tiny methods across 2 existing files:**\n- `Owner.setAddress` \u2014 now stores `AddressNormalizer.normalize(address)`, so the create path persists and `GET` returns the canonical form (mirrors `setTelephone`/`setEmail`). This is where \"normalize whenever an owner is created\" lands.\n- `OwnerUniqueHouseholdAdvice.householdId` and `isHouseholdTaken` \u2014 the address portion of the household key now uses `AddressNormalizer.normalize`, so both the shared household id and duplicate detection compare the normalized form (e.g. incoming `\"12 main st\"` matches a stored `\"12 MAIN STREET\"`).\n\n**Required-field check:** left untouched. Since normalization only removes whitespace, \"blank after normalization\" is exactly `String.isBlank()` on the raw value, which `OwnerRequiredFieldsAdvice.addIfBlank` already enforces \u2014 so the `\"   \"` \u2192 400 test passes without editing that class, avoiding a fourth touched file and the WMC cost of that larger advice class.\n\n**Tests:** all 3 acceptance tests (whitespace/case normalization, abbreviation expansion, blank-after-normalize rejection) pass, and the full `mvnw test` build is green.",
